exit 0
# From the ingress-nginx ModSecurity settings of Ingress shop/api.
apiVersion: waf.inkwall.dev/v1alpha1
kind: WAFRuleSet
metadata:
  name: api-modsecurity
  namespace: shop
spec:
  source:
    seclang: |
      # annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 2
      SecRule ARGS:debug "@streq true" "id:1100,phase:1,deny,status:403,msg:'debug switch'"
---
apiVersion: waf.inkwall.dev/v1alpha1
kind: WAFPolicy
metadata:
  name: api
  namespace: shop
spec:
  mode: Block
  ruleSets:
  - ref:
      kind: WAFRuleSet
      name: api-modsecurity
  targetRefs:
  - kind: Ingress
    name: api
--- stderr
note: no ConfigMap web/none in the files: ModSecurity is taken as off globally (only the annotations count)
Ingress shop/api: WAFPolicy shop/api (Block), WAFRuleSet shop/api-modsecurity
  mapped  annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 2: kept in the WAFRuleSet: SecRule ARGS:debug "@streq true" "id:1100,phase:1,deny,status:403,msg:'debug switch'"
  mapped  annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 1: SecRuleEngine On: mode: Block
  check   the Ingress has no class: assumed served by ingress-nginx
Ingress shop/other: no WAFPolicy
  check   ModSecurity is on but runs no rules besides its own configuration's: nothing to migrate
7 Ingress(es) read (5 of another class than traefik left out): 1 WAFPolicy, 1 WAFRuleSet; 0 setting(s) not migrated need a human (TODO)
